{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_delta","contentIndex":1,"delta":"{\"description\": \"Trace HEAD and refs\", \"prompt\": \"Other explorers are investigating different slices of the same subsystem in parallel. Don't try to cover everything. Focus on your assigned angle and go deep.\\n\\n## Question\\n\\n> Does this repository's git storage work end to end? Cover how HEAD, the refs, the index, and the object store fit together to produce README.md in the working tree.\\n\\n## Your Exploration Angle\\n\\nTrace HEAD and all reference resolution in this concrete repository: symbolic HEAD, loose or packed refs, the selected commit object, and its tree path to README.md. Verify object IDs and object types/content with read-only commands. Explain exactly what is present on disk and whether this slice is internally consistent.\\n\\n## Output\\n\\n### Components Found\\nThe key types, services, classes, and abstractions. For each: name, file path, and a one-sentence description of what it does.\\n\\n### Flow\\nThe execution flow step by step. For each step: what command/storage lookup occurs, where it reads, what it yields, and what comes next. Include object IDs.\\n\\n### Files Read\\nEvery file you read during exploration, so the explainer can reference them.\\n\\n### Boundaries\\nWhere this subsystem connects to the index, working tree, and object database.\\n\\n### Non-Obvious Things\\nAnything surprising or easy to get wrong.\\n\\n### Open Questions\\nAnything you couldn't fully trace or understand. Be honest about gaps.\", \"subagent_type\": \"generalPurpose\", \"model\": \"grok-4.7[effort=xhigh,fast=true]\", \"readonly\": true, \"run_in_background\": false}"}}
{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":1,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_b8f00374f24b42529927adfb072b7952|fc_0b3ed17c6d7d26f6016aef56e18f8887d0bf696df6e4fab6d3","name":"Task","arguments":{"description":"Trace HEAD and refs","prompt":"Other explorers are investigating different slices of the same subsystem in parallel. Don't try to cover everything. Focus on your assigned angle and go deep.\n\n## Question\n\n> Does this repository's git storage work end to end? Cover how HEAD, the refs, the index, and the object store fit together to produce README.md in the working tree.\n\n## Your Exploration Angle\n\nTrace HEAD and all reference resolution in this concrete repository: symbolic HEAD, loose or packed refs, the selected commit object, and its tree path to README.md. Verify object IDs and object types/content with read-only commands. Explain exactly what is present on disk and whether this slice is internally consistent.\n\n## Output\n\n### Components Found\nThe key types, services, classes, and abstractions. For each: name, file path, and a one-sentence description of what it does.\n\n### Flow\nThe execution flow step by step. For each step: what command/storage lookup occurs, where it reads, what it yields, and what comes next. Include object IDs.\n\n### Files Read\nEvery file you read during exploration, so the explainer can reference them.\n\n### Boundaries\nWhere this subsystem connects to the index, working tree, and object database.\n\n### Non-Obvious Things\nAnything surprising or easy to get wrong.\n\n### Open Questions\nAnything you couldn't fully trace or understand. Be honest about gaps.","subagent_type":"generalPurpose","model":"grok-4.7[effort=xhigh,fast=true]","readonly":true,"run_in_background":false}}}}
