{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_delta","contentIndex":2,"delta":"{\"description\": \"Decode index entry\", \"prompt\": \"Other explorers are investigating different slices of the same subsystem in parallel. Don't try to cover everything. Focus on your assigned angle and go deep.\\n\\n## Question\\n\\n> Does this repository's git storage work end to end? Cover how HEAD, the refs, the index, and the object store fit together to produce README.md in the working tree.\\n\\n## Your Exploration Angle\\n\\nInspect and decode this repository's .git/index, especially the README.md cache entry: format/version, path, stage, mode, blob object ID, stat metadata, extensions/checksum if relevant. Compare the index entry to HEAD's tree and the working-tree README.md using read-only Git/plumbing and binary inspection. Determine whether the index is valid and consistent.\\n\\n## Output\\n\\n### Components Found\\nThe key structures and files. For each: name, file path, and a one-sentence description.\\n\\n### Flow\\nWalk through how Git uses the index entry between HEAD/tree objects and the working file. Include concrete IDs and comparisons.\\n\\n### Files Read\\nEvery file you read during exploration.\\n\\n### Boundaries\\nConnections to refs, object database, and working tree.\\n\\n### Non-Obvious Things\\nSurprises and pitfalls.\\n\\n### Open Questions\\nAnything unresolved.\", \"subagent_type\": \"generalPurpose\", \"model\": \"grok-4.7[effort=xhigh,fast=true]\", \"readonly\": true, \"run_in_background\": false}"}}
{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":2,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_774c4c80ceef4a8996dd4bbf87b27f11|fc_0b3ed17c6d7d26f6016aef56f2e52487d0a26f11baebc71dac","name":"Task","arguments":{"description":"Decode index entry","prompt":"Other explorers are investigating different slices of the same subsystem in parallel. Don't try to cover everything. Focus on your assigned angle and go deep.\n\n## Question\n\n> Does this repository's git storage work end to end? Cover how HEAD, the refs, the index, and the object store fit together to produce README.md in the working tree.\n\n## Your Exploration Angle\n\nInspect and decode this repository's .git/index, especially the README.md cache entry: format/version, path, stage, mode, blob object ID, stat metadata, extensions/checksum if relevant. Compare the index entry to HEAD's tree and the working-tree README.md using read-only Git/plumbing and binary inspection. Determine whether the index is valid and consistent.\n\n## Output\n\n### Components Found\nThe key structures and files. For each: name, file path, and a one-sentence description.\n\n### Flow\nWalk through how Git uses the index entry between HEAD/tree objects and the working file. Include concrete IDs and comparisons.\n\n### Files Read\nEvery file you read during exploration.\n\n### Boundaries\nConnections to refs, object database, and working tree.\n\n### Non-Obvious Things\nSurprises and pitfalls.\n\n### Open Questions\nAnything unresolved.","subagent_type":"generalPurpose","model":"grok-4.7[effort=xhigh,fast=true]","readonly":true,"run_in_background":false}}}}
