{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_delta","contentIndex":3,"delta":"{\"description\": \"Trace object materialization\", \"prompt\": \"Other explorers are investigating different slices of the same subsystem in parallel. Don't try to cover everything. Focus on your assigned angle and go deep.\\n\\n## Question\\n\\n> Does this repository's git storage work end to end? Cover how HEAD, the refs, the index, and the object store fit together to produce README.md in the working tree.\\n\\n## Your Exploration Angle\\n\\nTrace the object database and working-tree materialization for README.md in this concrete repository. Inspect loose objects and/or packfiles, verify zlib/header/hash semantics where practical, follow commit -> tree -> blob, and compare the blob bytes to README.md. Also run read-only integrity/status checks to assess whether storage works end to end.\\n\\n## Output\\n\\n### Components Found\\nKey on-disk object-store components and what each does.\\n\\n### Flow\\nStep-by-step object lookup and conversion into README.md, with concrete object IDs, commands, and byte/content comparisons.\\n\\n### Files Read\\nEvery file read.\\n\\n### Boundaries\\nConnections to HEAD/refs and index.\\n\\n### Non-Obvious Things\\nSurprises, caveats, or misleading assumptions.\\n\\n### Open Questions\\nAnything unresolved.\", \"subagent_type\": \"generalPurpose\", \"model\": \"grok-4.7[effort=xhigh,fast=true]\", \"readonly\": true, \"run_in_background\": false}"}}
{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":3,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_a3b463c7310a467eb2b7513f14066760|fc_0b3ed17c6d7d26f6016aef56f2e52487d0afd1b0212a9af760","name":"Task","arguments":{"description":"Trace object materialization","prompt":"Other explorers are investigating different slices of the same subsystem in parallel. Don't try to cover everything. Focus on your assigned angle and go deep.\n\n## Question\n\n> Does this repository's git storage work end to end? Cover how HEAD, the refs, the index, and the object store fit together to produce README.md in the working tree.\n\n## Your Exploration Angle\n\nTrace the object database and working-tree materialization for README.md in this concrete repository. Inspect loose objects and/or packfiles, verify zlib/header/hash semantics where practical, follow commit -> tree -> blob, and compare the blob bytes to README.md. Also run read-only integrity/status checks to assess whether storage works end to end.\n\n## Output\n\n### Components Found\nKey on-disk object-store components and what each does.\n\n### Flow\nStep-by-step object lookup and conversion into README.md, with concrete object IDs, commands, and byte/content comparisons.\n\n### Files Read\nEvery file read.\n\n### Boundaries\nConnections to HEAD/refs and index.\n\n### Non-Obvious Things\nSurprises, caveats, or misleading assumptions.\n\n### Open Questions\nAnything unresolved.","subagent_type":"generalPurpose","model":"grok-4.7[effort=xhigh,fast=true]","readonly":true,"run_in_background":false}}}}
