MzVJWvlRqVHTyMNBky1U0C126o4vxossJpsYnvZyyAdl98XNqYJok6EAThbsXsjyM6JPJ4xGAAlOPw4kWIZUrgPhR2FyKPrLNsU6AoPt8xQZcMd_W53KlDn58KvjBfpNMcN1KMNPAoKNRCFDI7FH1i9ItYZIk0hWYqstziHnNgrESRUONMhDmSQBeF7rjOGoEUanmGtqzPYDPnwWwkw0zb8NOjyoS-cisxET1QUJmAOuZpuFZAuGEYfzal1egrM73hKQXfQE4iTPLriGw8ECiAdV72k-EFLv--n4Yjnc15l1iZXT3qo6acts7YesF557X7Qawb0Q==\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_b8f00374f24b42529927adfb072b7952|fc_0b3ed17c6d7d26f6016aef56e18f8887d0bf696df6e4fab6d3","name":"Task","arguments":{"description":"Trace HEAD and refs","prompt":"Other explorers are investigating different slices of the same subsystem in parallel. Don't try to cover everything. Focus on your assigned angle and go deep.\n\n## Question\n\n> Does this repository's git storage work end to end? Cover how HEAD, the refs, the index, and the object store fit together to produce README.md in the working tree.\n\n## Your Exploration Angle\n\nTrace HEAD and all reference resolution in this concrete repository: symbolic HEAD, loose or packed refs, the selected commit object, and its tree path to README.md. Verify object IDs and object types/content with read-only commands. Explain exactly what is present on disk and whether this slice is internally consistent.\n\n## Output\n\n### Components Found\nThe key types, services, classes, and abstractions. For each: name, file path, and a one-sentence description of what it does.\n\n### Flow\nThe execution flow step by step. For each step: what command/storage lookup occurs, where it reads, what it yields, and what comes next. Include object IDs.\n\n### Files Read\nEvery file you read during exploration, so the explainer can reference them.\n\n### Boundaries\nWhere this subsystem connects to the index, working tree, and object database.\n\n### Non-Obvious Things\nAnything surprising or easy to get wrong.\n\n### Open Questions\nAnything you couldn't fully trace or understand. Be honest about gaps.","subagent_type":"generalPurpose","model":"grok-4.7[effort=xhigh,fast=true]","readonly":true,"run_in_background":false}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_774c4c80ceef4a8996dd4bbf87b27f11|fc_0b3ed17c6d7d26f6016aef56f2e52487d0a26f11baebc71dac","name":"Task","arguments":{"description":"Decode index entry","prompt":"Other explorers are investigating different slices of the same subsystem in parallel. Don't try to cover everything. Focus on your assigned angle and go deep.\n\n## Question\n\n> Does this repository's git storage work end to end? Cover how HEAD, the refs, the index, and the object store fit together to produce README.md in the working tree.\n\n## Your Exploration Angle\n\nInspect and decode this repository's .git/index, especially the README.md cache entry: format/version, path, stage, mode, blob object ID, stat metadata, extensions/checksum if relevant. Compare the index entry to HEAD's tree and the working-tree README.md using read-only Git/plumbing and binary inspection. Determine whether the index is valid and consistent.\n\n## Output\n\n### Components Found\nThe key structures and files. For each: name, file path, and a one-sentence description.\n\n### Flow\nWalk through how Git uses the index entry between HEAD/tree objects and the working file. Include concrete IDs and comparisons.\n\n### Files Read\nEvery file you read during exploration.\n\n### Boundaries\nConnections to refs, object database, and working tree.\n\n### Non-Obvious Things\nSurprises and pitfalls.\n\n### Open Questions\nAnything unresolved.","subagent_type":"generalPurpose","model":"grok-4.7[effort=xhigh,fast=true]","readonly":true,"run_in_background":false}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_a3b463c7310a467eb2b7513f14066760|fc_0b3ed17c6d7d26f6016aef56f2e52487d0afd1b0212a9af760","name":"Task","arguments":{"description":"Trace object materialization","prompt":"Other explorers are investigating different slices of the same subsystem in parallel. Don't try to cover everything. Focus on your assigned angle and go deep.\n\n## Question\n\n> Does this repository's git storage work end to end? Cover how HEAD, the refs, the index, and the object store fit together to produce README.md in the working tree.\n\n## Your Exploration Angle\n\nTrace the object database and working-tree materialization for README.md in this concrete repository. Inspect loose objects and/or packfiles, verify zlib/header/hash semantics where practical, follow commit -> tree -> blob, and compare the blob bytes to README.md. Also run read-only integrity/status checks to assess whether storage works end to end.\n\n## Output\n\n### Components Found\nKey on-disk object-store components and what each does.\n\n### Flow\nStep-by-step object lookup and conversion into README.md, with concrete object IDs, commands, and byte/content comparisons.\n\n### Files Read\nEvery file read.\n\n### Boundaries\nConnections to HEAD/refs and index.\n\n### Non-Obvious Things\nSurprises, caveats, or misleading assumptions.\n\n### Open Questions\nAnything unresolved.","subagent_type":"generalPurpose","model":"grok-4.7[effort=xhigh,fast=true]","readonly":true,"run_in_background":false}}],"api":"openai-responses","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","usage":{"input":157,"output":1148,"cacheRead":17280,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":162,"totalTokens":18585,"cost":{"input":0.000628,"output":0.02296,"cacheRead":0.006912000000000001,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.030500000000000003,"totalFromProvider":false}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794070234380,"responseId":"resp_0b3ed17c6d7d26f6016aef56daf10887d0aa0525124658c564","rawStopReason":"completed","durationMs":24764,"thinkingLevel":"medium"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_b8f00374f24b42529927adfb072b7952|fc_0b3ed17c6d7d26f6016aef56e18f8887d0bf696df6e4fab6d3","toolName":"Task","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Invalid model selection \"grok-4.7[effort=xhigh,fast=true]\". Model could not be resolved to a valid subagent model.\nAllowed model slugs:\n- inherit\n- deepseek/deepseek-flash (thinking: off, low, high, max)\n- deepseek