{"type":"tool_execution_update","toolCallId":"call_15e2231873bd40919be56f75ba440687|fc_0b3ed17c6d7d26f6016aef57066e9887d09773657d0fefff84","toolName":"Task","args":{"description":"Decode index entry","prompt":"Other explorers are investigating different slices of the same subsystem in parallel. Don't try to cover everything. Focus on your assigned angle and go deep.\n\n## Question\n\n> Does this repository's git storage work end to end? Cover how HEAD, the refs, the index, and the object store fit together to produce README.md in the working tree.\n\n## Your Exploration Angle\n\nInspect and decode this repository's .git/index, especially the README.md cache entry: format/version, path, stage, mode, blob object ID, stat metadata, extensions/checksum if relevant. Compare the index entry to HEAD's tree and the working-tree README.md using read-only Git/plumbing and binary inspection. Determine whether the index is valid and consistent.\n\n## Output\n\n### Components Found\nThe key structures and files. For each: name, file path, and a one-sentence description.\n\n### Flow\nWalk through how Git uses the index entry between HEAD/tree objects and the working file. Include concrete IDs and comparisons.\n\n### Files Read\nEvery file you read during exploration.\n\n### Boundaries\nConnections to refs, object database, and working tree.\n\n### Non-Obvious Things\nSurprises and pitfalls.\n\n### Open Questions\nAnything unresolved.","subagent_type":"generalPurpose","model":"inherit","readonly":true,"run_in_background":false},"partialResult":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Running: 12 steps\n· find: .git/objects\n· bash: pwd\n· read: .git/refs/heads/main\n· read: .git/config"}],"details":{"agentId":"e7262793-a041-450d-aed4-3d9669100c7f","forkedFrom":null,"subagentType":"generalPurpose","model":{"provider":"openai","id":"gpt-5.6-sol","thinking":"medium"},"readonly":true,"background":false,"status":"running","transcript":"/var/folders/11/m_kwnqr97632l_cjt0mhytvh0000gn/T/pstack-