{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_3e3826f62378446db66848e4058506b4|fc_0b3ed17c6d7d26f6016aef57066e9887d08372ac72fbcefe96","toolName":"Task","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This is the output of the subagent:\n\nresponse:\n<response>\n## Components Found\n\n- **Symbolic HEAD** — `.git/HEAD`\n  - Contains `ref: refs/heads/main`.\n- **Branch ref** — `.git/refs/heads/main`\n  - Contains commit ID `d9722409cabd904e7339fda14fe1818d77be6641`.\n- **Loose object database** — `.git/objects/<first-two-hex>/<remaining-38-hex>`\n  - Commit: `.git/objects/d9/722409cabd904e7339fda14fe1818d77be6641`\n  - Tree: `.git/objects/7e/476488da437541819d424ac7276cf48b3491a6`\n  - Blob: `.git/objects/8c/1828de80f220d2d9d841f6d6380c29e1a9bc54`\n- **Pack storage** — `.git/objects/pack/`\n  - Empty. All repository objects are loose.\n- **Index** — `.git/index`\n  - Binary `DIRC` format, version 2, with one entry: `README.md`.\n  - The entry has mode `100644`, size `34`, and blob ID `8c1828de80f220d2d9d841f6d6380c29e1a9bc54`.\n  - Its cached-tree extension contains tree ID `7e476488da437541819d424ac7276cf48b3491a6`.\n- **Working-tree file** — `README.md`\n  - Contains exactly:\n    ```text\n    # Unchanged prompt corpus fixture\n    ```\n\n## Flow\n\n1. Git reads `.git/HEAD`:\n   ```text\n   ref: refs/heads/main\n   ```\n\n2. It follows `.git/refs/heads/main` to:\n   ```text\n   d9722409cabd904e7339fda14fe1818d77be6641\n   ```\n\n3. The commit is stored as the loose object:\n   ```text\n   .git/objects/d9/722409cabd904e7339fda14fe1818d77be6641\n   ```\n\n   The file begins with a valid zlib stream marker (`0x78 0x01`). Loose objects are zlib-compressed bytes whose decompressed form is:\n\n   ```text\n   commit <decimal-size>\\0<payload>\n   ```\n\n   This initial commit points to tree:\n\n   ```text\n   7e476488da437541819d424ac7276cf48b3491a6\n   ```\n\n   The reflog and `COMMIT_EDITMSG` identify it as the initial commit, message `Initial fixture`.\n\n4. The root tree is the loose object:\n   ```text\n   .git/objects/7e/476488da437541819d424ac7276cf48b3491a6\n   ```\n\n   Its uncompressed object framing is:\n\n   ```text\n   tree 37\\0\n   ```\n\n   The 37-byte payload is one binary tree entry:\n\n   ```text\n   100644 README.md\\0<20-byte blob object ID>\n   ```\n\n   Its blob ID is:\n\n   ```text\n   8c1828de80f220d2d9d841f6d6380c29e1a9bc54\n   ```\n\n   The payload size is consistent: six mode bytes, one space, nine filename bytes, one NUL, and twenty raw object-ID bytes = 37.\n\n5. The blob is stored at:\n   ```text\n   .git/objects/8c/1828de80f220d2d9d841f6d6380c29e1a9bc54\n   ```\n\n   Its compressed bytes visibly decode to the standard header and content:\n\n   ```text\n   blob 34\\0# Unchanged prompt corpus fixture\\n\n   ```\n\n   The payload is 34 bytes:\n\n   ```text\n   # Unchanged prompt corpus fixture\\n\n   ```\n\n6. The working-tree `README.md` has the same content and terminating newline. Thus the materialization path is:\n\n   ```text\n   HEAD\n     → refs/heads/main\n     → commit d9722409…\n     → tree 7e476488…\n     → README.md blob 8c1828de…\n     → 34-byte working-tree README.md\n   ```\n\n7. The index independently agrees with the object chain:\n   - one `README.md` entry\n   - mode `100644`\n   - size `34`\n   - blob `8c1828de…`\n   - cached root tree `7e476488…`\n\nUseful read-only commands for reproducing these checks are:\n\n```sh\ngit rev-parse HEAD\ngit rev-parse HEAD^{tree}\ngit rev-parse HEAD:README.md\ngit ls-tree HEAD README.md\ngit cat-file -p HEAD\ngit cat-file -p HEAD^{tree}\ngit cat-file -p HEAD:README.md\ngit cat-file -s HEAD:README.md\ngit hash-object README.md\ngit ls-files --stage README.md\ngit status --short\ngit fsck --full\n```\n\nExpected central results:\n\n```text\nHEAD             d9722409cabd904e7339fda14fe1818d77be6641\nHEAD^{tree}      7e476488da437541819d424ac7276cf48b3491a6\nHEAD:README.md   8c1828de80f220d2d9d841f6d6380c29e1a9bc54\n```\n\n## Files Read\n\n- `README.md`\n- `.git/HEAD`\n- `.git/config`\n- `.git/index`\n- `.git/refs/heads/main`\n- `.git/logs/HEAD`\n- `.git/logs/refs/heads/main`\n- `.git/COMMIT_EDITMSG`\n- `.git/description`\n- `.git/info/exclude`\n- `.git/objects/d9/722409cabd904e7339fda14fe1818d77be6641`\n- `.git/objects/7e/476488da437541819d424ac7276cf48b3491a6`\n- `.git/objects/8c/1828de80f220d2d9d841f6d6380c29e1a9bc54`\n\nDirectories inspected:\n\n- `.git/`\n- `.git/refs/`\n- `.git/refs/heads/`\n- `.git/objects/`\n- `.git/objects/pack/`\n\n## Boundaries\n\n- **HEAD and refs:** HEAD does not hold an object ID directly; it names `refs/heads/main`, which holds the commit ID.\n- **Refs and object store:** The branch ref selects the commit object. The commit selects a root tree; the tree maps `README.md` to its blob.\n- **Index and object store:** The index directly records the staged blob ID. It does not store README’s contents. Its cached-tree extension also records the root tree ID.\n- **Index and working tree:** Git compares the index entry’s metadata/content identity against `README.md` to detect unstaged changes.\n- **Commit versus index:** The commit’s tree and the index’s cached tree agree, while the index blob and working file agree. This is the storage configuration expected for a clean checkout.\n\n## Non-Obvious Things\n\n- Object filenames are not arbitrary. For SHA-1 repositories, Git hashes:\n  ```text\n  <type> <payload-length>\\0<payload>\n  ```\n  The resulting 40-character ID is split into a two-character directory and 38-character filename.\n- The blob ID is a hash of the framed blob—not merely the 34 README payload bytes.\n- Tree object IDs are stored as raw 20-byte values inside tree payloads, not as 40-byte hexadecimal text.\n- The index is neither a copy of the working tree nor a commit. It is a staged pathname-to-blob/mode mapping plus stat and cache data.\n- `.git/objects/pack/` being empty is not a problem. This tiny repository has exactly the loose commit, tree, and blob needed for the initial snapshot.\n- The timestamps in the reflogs are in the future relative to many ordinary repositories (`1793923200`, November 2026), but that does not affect object lookup or content integrity.\n- The repository uses the normal SHA-1 object layout; there is no evidence of SHA-256 storage, alternates, replacement objects, or packed refs.\n\n## Open Questions\n\nThe repository artifacts form a complete and internally consistent end-to-end storage chain. However, the execution sandbox failed before every attempted `git status`/`git fsck` command with:\n\n```text\nno verified OS sandbox is available: listen EINVAL ...srt-mux-....sock\n```\n\nTherefore:\n\n- `git fsck --full` could not be executed to independently recompute every object hash.\n- `git status --short` could not be executed as a final porcelain-level cleanliness check.\n- The conclusions above come from direct inspection of HEAD, the ref, index bytes, loose zlib object files, and working-tree bytes.\n\nNo repository inconsistency was found; the remaining uncertainty is limited to the unavailable command-level integrity run, not a missing link in the stored object chain.\n</response>\n\nAgent ID: 9b789b31-315b-4824-88ab-aa419512a894 (can be used with the `resume` parameter to send a follow-up after it completes)"}],"details":{"agentId":"9b789b31-315b-4824-88ab-aa419512a894","forkedFrom":null,"subagentType":"generalPurpose","model":{"provider":"openai","id":"gpt-5.6-sol","thinking":"medium"},"readonly":true,"background":false,"status":"success","transcript":"/var/folders/11/m_kwnqr97632l_cjt0mhytvh0000gn/T/pstack-corpus-ur5cbW/21-PROMPT-HOW-READONLY-EXPLORERS-r2/pi/home/.pi/agent/pstack/workspaces/--private-var-folders-11-m_kwnqr97632l_cjt0mhytvh0000gn-T-pstack-corpus-ur5cbW-21-PROMPT-HOW-READONLY-EXPLORERS-r2-pi-work--/subagents/2026-11-07T16-51-18-820Z_9b789b31-315b-4824-88ab-aa419512a894.jsonl","pid":null,"machine":null,"description":"Trace object materialization"},"usage":{"input":10097,"outpu