488... at .git/objects/7e/..., and README blob 8c1828de... at .git/objects/8c/.... The tree payload is 37 bytes: `100644 README.md\\0<20-byte blob id>`. The blob payload is 34 bytes: `# Unchanged prompt corpus fixture\\n`. All objects are loose; .git/objects/pack is empty. The index independently records blob 8c1828... and cached tree 7e4764....\n\nAll explorers report the command sandbox prevented running Git commands like git fsck/status/hash-object, so direct file/binary inspection was used. You have read-only access and should resolve the object-ID contradiction by checking repository files directly if possible. Be explicit about verification limits: distinguish direct structural evidence from unavailable command-level fsck/status verification.\n\n## Instructions\n\nThe explorers each investigated a different angle of the same subsystem. Their findings overlap and one has a contradiction. Reconcile them by checking code/storage yourself. Merge the slices into a unified picture.\n\nWrite an explanation a senior engineer unfamiliar with Git internals could read and walk away with a solid mental model, understanding architecture well enough to work with it confidently.\n\n## Output Format\n\nUse this structure, adapted as needed:\n\n### Overview\n1-2 paragraphs with a direct yes/no assessment.\n\n### Key Concepts\nBrief definitions of HEAD, refs, commit/tree/blob objects, index, working tree.\n\n### How It Works\nWalk concrete flow step by step with exact IDs and paths. Include a mermaid or ASCII diagram. Explain both committed-snapshot path and index/working-tree comparison path; clarify that checkout writes blobs to files but current artifacts prove consistency rather than recording historical checkout execution.\n\n### Where Things Live\nBrief path map.\n\n### Gotchas\nNon-obvious details and verification caveat.\n\nUse concrete language. Do not dump annotated source. Do not overclaim checks that could not run.","subagent_type":"generalPurpose","model":"claude-opus-5-5:xhigh","readonly":true,"run_in_background":false}}],"api":"openai-responses","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","usage":{"input":6839,"output":932,"cacheRead":22400,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":96,"totalTokens":30171,"cost":{"input":0.027356,"output":0.01864,"cacheRead":0.008960000000000001,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.054956,"totalFromProvider":false}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794070397282,"responseId":"resp_0b3ed17c6d7d26f6016aef577de11087d0a98a9fc5527373da","rawStopReason":"completed","durationMs":20843,"thinkingLevel":"medium"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_3d26c65ad3334d30a2cda2cde7e9b2f3|fc_0b3ed17c6d7d26f6016aef57830d9887d09f1809978398bbc6","toolName":"Task","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Invalid model selection \"claude-opus-5-5:xhigh\". Model could not be resolved to a valid subagent model.\nAllowed model slugs:\n- inherit\n- deepseek/deepseek-flash (thinking: off, low, high, max)\n- deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro (thinking: off, high, max)\n- openai/chat-latest (thinking: off, minimal, low, medium, high)\n- openai/gpt-4\n- openai/gpt-4-turbo\n- openai/gpt-4.1\n- openai/gpt-4.1-mini\n- openai/gpt-4.1-nano\n- openai/gpt-4o\n- openai/gpt-4o-2024-05-13\n- openai/gpt-4o-2024-08-06\n- openai/gpt-4o-2024-11-20\n- openai/gpt-4o-mini\n- openai/gpt-5 (thinking: minimal, low, medium, high)\n- openai/gpt-5-chat-latest\n- openai/gpt-5-mini (thinking: minimal, low, medium, high)\n- openai/gpt-5-nano (thinking: minimal, low, medium, high)\n- openai/gpt-5-pro (thinking: high)\n- openai/gpt-5.1 (thinking: off, low, medium, high)\n- openai/gpt-5.2 (thinking: off, low, medium, high, xhigh)\n- openai/gpt-5.2-pro (thinking: medium, high, xhigh)\n- openai/gpt-5.3-codex (thinking: off, low, medium, high, xhigh)\n- openai/gpt-5.3-codex-spark (thinking: low, medium, high, xhigh)\n- openai/gpt-5.4 (thinking: off, low, medium, high, xhigh)\n- openai/gpt-5.4-mini (thinking: off, low, medium, high, xhigh)\n- openai/gpt-5.4-nano (thinking: off, low, medium, high, xhigh)\n- openai/gpt-5.4-pro (thinking: medium, high, xhigh)\n- openai/gpt-5.5 (thinking: off, low, medium, high, xhigh)\n- openai/gpt-5.5-pro (thinking: medium, high, xhigh)\n- openai/gpt-5.6-cyber (thinking: low, medium, high, xhigh, max)\n- openai/gpt-5.6-luna (thinking: off, low, medium, high, xhigh, max)\n- openai/gpt-5.6-sol (thinking: off, low, medium, high, xhigh, max)\n- openai/gpt-5.6-terra (thinking: off, low, medium, high, xhigh, max)\n- openai/gpt-6-astra (thinking: low, medium, high, xhigh, max)\n- openai/gpt-6-luna (thinking: off, low, medium, high, xhigh, max)\n- openai/gpt-6-sol (thinking: off, low, medium, high, xhigh, max)\n- openai/gpt-6.1-sol (thinking: low, medium, high, xhigh, max)\n- openai/gpt-6.1-terra (thinking: off, low, medium, high, xhigh, max)\n- openai/gpt-daybreak-blue-latest (thinking: off, low, medium, high, xhigh, max)\n- openai/gpt-daybreak-red-latest (thinking: off, low, medium, high, xhigh, max)\n- openai/o1 (thinking: low, medium, high)\n- openai/o1-pro (thinking: low, medium, high)\n- openai/o3 (thinking: low, medium, high)\n- openai/o3-mini (thinking: low, medium, high)\n- openai/o3-pro (thinking: low, medium, high)\n- openai/o4-mini (thinking: low, medium, high)\n\nAdd a thinking level as <model>:<level>, for example claude-opus-5-5:xhigh, or as <model>[effort=<level>].\nThe `model` parameter is optional. If omitted, the subagent uses the same model as the parent agent."}],"details":{},"isError":true,"durationMs":0,"timestamp":1794070418125},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Implementing inherit fallback strategy**","thinkingSignature":"{\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"id\":\"rs_0b3ed17c6d7d26f6016aef579451b087d0bcca69a7ca93b99f\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Implementing inherit fallback strategy**\"}],\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABq71eUZ07OyJIjCjHyrbp-G4LafNsTmjGHbGFRC8I5Nf0QPN-ipsR6JpMBKKzI6sRfePQZeJEzdU4NMnS-0VOEcmdtzRjIgzRRI97-LdJGVMRbTaqmbWSFFHqr1F-J0