t":"You are writing an architectural explanation for a senior engineer. Multiple explorer agents have traced different slices of the codebase in parallel and gathered findings. Synthesize their findings into one coherent, well-structured explanation.\n\n## Original Question\n\n> Does this repository's git storage work end to end? Cover how HEAD, the refs, the index, and the object store fit together to produce README.md in the working tree.\n\n## Explorer Findings\n\nExplorer 1 (HEAD/refs) found symbolic HEAD -> refs/heads/main -> commit d9722409cabd904e7339fda14fe1818d77be6641, with no packed-refs and all objects loose. It reported commit -> tree 8c1828... -> blob 7e4764..., but this conflicts with the other two explorers and likely reverses tree/blob IDs. It found the working file has 34 bytes and the index is v2 with one entry.\n\nExplorer 2 (index) decoded .git/index as DIRC v2, one stage-0 README.md entry, mode 100644, size 34, blob 8c1828de80f220d2d9d841f6d6380c29e1a9bc54. The TREE extension caches root tree 7e476488da437541819d424ac7276cf48b3491a6. It found a structurally present 20-byte checksum trailer. It traced HEAD commit d9722409... -> tree 7e476488... -> README blob 8c1828de..., matching index and working file.\n\nExplorer 3 (object store) independently found commit d9722409... at .git/objects/d9/..., root tree 7e476488... at .git/objects/7e/..., and README blob 8c1828de... at .git/objects/8c/.... The tree payload is 37 bytes: `100644 README.md\\0<20-byte blob id>`. The blob payload is 34 bytes: `# Unchanged prompt corpus fixture\\n`. All objects are loose; .git/objects/pack is empty. The index independently records blob 8c1828... and cached tree 7e4764....\n\nAll explorers report the command sandbox prevented running Git commands like git fsck/status/hash-object, so direct file/binary inspection was used. You have read-only access and should resolve the object-ID contradiction by checking repository files directly if possible. Be explicit about verification limits: distinguish direct structural evidence from unavailable command-level fsck/status verification.\n\n## Instructions\n\nThe explorers each investigated a different angle of the same subsystem. Their findings overlap and one has a contradiction. Reconcile them by checking code/storage yourself. Merge the slices into a unified picture.\n\nWrite an explanation a senior engineer unfamiliar with Git internals could read and walk away with a solid mental model, understanding architecture well enough to work with it confidently.\n\n## Output Format\n\nUse this structure, adapted as needed:\n\n### Overview\n1-2 paragraphs with a direct yes/no assessment.\n\n### Key Concepts\nBrief definitions of HEAD, refs, commit/tree/blob objects, index, working tree.\n\n### How It Works\nWalk concrete flow step by step with exact IDs and paths. Include a mermaid or ASCII diagram. Explain both committed-snapshot path and index/working-tree comparison path; clarify that checkout writes blobs to files but current artifacts prove consistency rather than recording historical checkout execution.\n\n### Where Things Live\nBrief path map.\n\n### Gotchas\nNon-obvious details and verification caveat.\n\nUse concrete language. Do not dump annotated source. Do not overclaim checks that could not run.","subagent_type":"generalPurpose","model":"inherit","readonly":true,"run_in_background":false}}],"api":"openai-responses","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","usage":{"input":1068,"output":839,"cacheRead":30080,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":12,"totalTokens":31987,"cost":{"input":0.004272,"output":0.01678,"cacheRead":0.012032000000000001,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.033084,"totalFromProvider":false}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794070418127,"responseId":"resp_0b3ed17c6d7d26f6016aef5792bb1087d0889cbc6f6d6368a1","rawStopReason":"completed","durationMs":18079,"thinkingLevel":"medium"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_218502028f9d4d3095f5f15576429dd2|fc_0b3ed17c6d7d26f6016aef5794c02087d085b4a416331679c5","toolName":"Task","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This is the output of the subagent:\n\nresponse:\n<response>\n### Overview\n\n**Yes—the repository’s Git storage is internally coherent end to end for the current `README.md`.** `HEAD` resolves through the `main` branch ref to commit `d9722409…`; that commit names root tree `7e476488…`; the tree maps `README.md` to blob `8c1828de…`; and that blob contains the same 34 bytes currently present in the working-tree file. The index independently records the same blob for a stage-0 `README.md` entry and caches the same root tree.\n\nThe conflicting report from Explorer 1 reversed the tree and blob IDs. Direct inspection confirms that the files exist at their expected loose-object paths, and the index’s binary contents visibly contain the blob and cached-tree IDs. The independently decoded object headers and payloads establish the correct mapping:\n\n- **Tree:** `7e476488da437541819d424ac7276cf48b3491a6`\n- **Blob:** `8c1828de80f220d2d9d841f6d6380c29e1a9bc54`\n\nThis establishes structural and content consistency. It does **not** prove that a checkout command historically produced the file, nor could command-level checks such as `git fsck`, `git status`, or `git hash-object` be run in the sandbox.\n\n### Key Concepts\n\n- **HEAD** — Identifies what is currently checked out. Here it is symbolic: it points to the `main` branch rather than directly to a commit.\n- **Ref** — A named pointer to an object ID, usually a commit. `refs/heads/main` stores the current tip of the `main` branch.\n- **Commit object** — Records snapshot metadata and points to a root tree. It does not directly contain file contents.\n- **Tree object** — Represents a directory. Each entry contains a mode, name, and object ID for a blob or another tree.\n- **Blob object** — Stores raw file bytes. It does not store the filename; the tree supplies the name.\n- **Index** — Git’s proposed next snapshot, often called the staging area. It stores paths, modes, object IDs, and cached filesystem metadata—not file contents.\n- **Working tree** — The ordinary files visible outside `.git`, including `README.md`.\n\n### How It Works\n\n#### 1. The committed-snapshot path\n\nThe current snapshot resolves as follows:\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    H[\".git/HEAD<br/>ref: refs/heads/main\"]\n    R[\".git/refs/heads/main<br/>d9722409...\"]\n    C[\"Commit d9722409...\"]\n    T[\"Tree 7e476488...\"]\n    E[\"100644 README.md<br/>→ blob 8c1828de...\"]\n    B[\"Blob 8c1828de...<br/>34-byte payload\"]\n    W[\"Working tree: README.md<br/># Unchanged prompt corpus fixture\\\\n\"]\n\n    H --> R\n    R --> C\n    C -->|tree field| T\n    T --> E\n    E --> B\n    B -. \"checkout materializes these bytes\" .-> W\n```\n\nConcretely:\n\n1. **HEAD selects the branch**\n\n   `.git/HEAD` contains:\n\n   ```text\n   ref: refs/heads/main\n   ```\n\n2. **The branch selects the commit**\n\n   `.git/refs/heads/main` contains:\n\n   ```text\n   d9722409cabd904e7339fda14fe1818d77be6641\n   ```\n\n   There is no `.git/packed-refs`, so this branch ref is stored as a loose ref.\n\n3. **The commit selects the root tree**\n\n   The loose commit object is stored at:\n\n   ```text\n   .git/objects/d9/722409cabd904e7339fda14fe1818d77be6641\n   ```\n\n   After decompression, its commit payload names:\n\n   ```text\n   tree 7e476488da437541819d424ac7276cf48b3491a6\n   ```\n\n4. **The root tree maps the filename to its blob**\n\n   The loose tree object is at:\n\n   ```text\n   .git/objects/7e/476488da437541819d424ac7276cf48b3491a6\n   ```\n\n   Its 37-byte payload consists of one tree entry:\n\n   ```text\n   100644 README.md\\0<20-byte binary object ID>\n   ```\n\n   The binary object ID is:\n\n   ```text\n   8c1828de80f220d2d9d841f6d6380c29e1a9bc54\n   ```\n\n   This is decisive in resolving the explorers’ contradiction: `7e476488…` is the **tree**, while `8c1828de…` is the **README blob**.\n\n5. **The blob supplies the file bytes**\n\n   The blob is stored at:\n\n   ```text\n   .git/objects/8c/1828de80f220d2d9d841f6d6380c29e1a9bc54\n   ```\n\n   Its object header identifies it as a 34-byte blob, and its payload is:\n\n   ```text\n   # Unchanged prompt corpus fixture\\n\n   ```\n\n6. **The working-tree file has those same bytes**\n\n   `README.md` is 34 bytes and reads:\n\n   ```markdown\n   # Unchanged prompt corpus fixture\n   ```\n\n   including the final newline.\n\nConceptually, checkout follows the commit-to-tree-to-blob chain and writes the blob payload under the pathname supplied by the tree. The current artifacts prove that the resulting file is consistent with such a checkout. They do not record or prove that a particular historical checkout invocation created it.\n\n#### 2. The index and working-tree comparison path\n\n`.git/index` is a `DIRC` version 2 index with one entry:\n\n| Field | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Path | `README.md` |\n| Stage | `0` |\n| Mode | `100644` |\n| Recorded size | `34` |\n| Blob | `8c1828de80f220d2d9d841f6d6380c29e1a9bc54` |\n\nStage 0 means this is a normal, fully resolved entry. Higher stages are used for unresolved merge conflicts.\n\nThe index therefore agrees with the committed snapshot:\n\n```text\nHEAD tree's README.md blob = 8c1828de...\nindex README.md blob      = 8c1828de...\n```\n\nThat means there is no staged content difference between `HEAD` and the index for this path.\n\nThe index also agrees with the working tree:\n\n```text\nindex recorded size       = 34 bytes\nworking README.md size    = 34 bytes\nblob payload              = working file's 34 bytes\n```\n\nIn normal operation, Git initially uses the index’s cached filesystem metadata to make status checks inexpensive. If those stat fields do not conclusively show that a file is unchanged, Git reads and hashes the working file and compares the resulting blob ID with the index entry. The index itself contains the blob ID, not a duplicate of the file contents.\n\nThe index has a `TREE` extension caching:\n\n```text\n7e476488da437541819d424ac7276cf48b3491a6\n```\n\nThat is the same root tree named by the commit. This extension is an optimization for constructing trees efficiently; the ordinary index entries remain the authoritative description of the staged paths.\n\nThus all three relevant views align:\n\n```text\nCommitted snapshot: README.md → blob 8c1828de...\nIndex:             README.md → blob 8c1828de...\nWorking tree:      README.md = corresponding 34-byte payload\n```\n\n### Where Things Live\n\n| Purpose | Path |\n|---|---|\n| Current checkout pointer | `.git/HEAD` |\n| `main` branch ref | `.git/refs/heads/main` |\n| Commit object | `.git/objects/d9/722409cabd904e7339fda14fe1818d77be6641` |\n| Root tree object | `.git/objects/7e/476488da437541819d424ac7276cf48b3491a6` |\n| README blob object | `.git/objects/8c/1828de80f220d2d9d841f6d6380c29e1a9bc54` |\n| Staging index | `.git/index` |\n| Working file | `README.md` |\n| Pack directory | `.git/objects/pack/` — empty |\n| Packed refs | `.git/packed-refs` — absent |\n\nAll three objects are loose. Git splits each object ID into a two-character directory and a 38-character filename; for example, `8c1828…` becomes `.git/objects/8c/1828…`.\n\n### Gotchas\n\n- **The tree owns the filename.** The blob contains only `README.md`’s bytes; it does not know that it is called `README.md`.\n- **The index does not store staged file content inline.** It points to the staged blob in the object store and supplements that with mode and stat-cache information.\n- **The index `TREE` extension is a cache.** Its agreement with the commit tree is useful corroboration, but Git can reconstruct a tree from the ordinary index entries.\n- **Object IDs are encoded in binary inside trees and the index.** They are not stored there as 40 printable hexadecimal characters.\n- **Object type is part of hashing.** A blob ID is derived from a representation such as `blob 34\\0` followed by the 34 payload bytes, not from the payload alone.\n- **The earlier ID conflict is resolved.** `7e476488…` is unambiguously the root tree, and `8c1828de…` is the README blob. The commit’s tree field, the tree entry, the index entry, and the index `TREE` extension all support that assignment.\n- **Verification was storage-level, not Git-command-level.** Direct inspection confirmed `HEAD`, the branch ref, `README.md`, the loose object paths, the absence of `packed-refs`, the empty pack directory, and the index structure. The explorers independently decompressed and decoded the objects and index. However, the sandbox prevented running `git fsck`, `git status`, `git hash-object`, or equivalent Git commands. Therefore the strongest justified conclusion is: **the inspected storage graph and contents are mutually consistent**, but no claim is made that Git’s full integrity checker or porcelain status command was successfully executed.\n</response>\n\nAgent ID: f94933cf-6841-47c2-b6b2-246475f7e87c (can be used with the `resume` parameter to send a follow-up after it completes)"}],"details":{"agentId":"f94933cf-6841-47c2-b6b2-246475f7e87c","forkedFrom":null,"subagentType":"generalPurpose","model":{"provider":"openai","id":"gpt-5.6-sol","thinking":"medium"},"readonly":true,"background":false,"status":"success","transcript":"/var/folders/11/m_kwnqr97632l_cjt0mhytvh0000gn/T/pstack-corpus-ur5cbW/21-PROMPT-HOW-READONLY-EXPLORERS-r2/pi/home/.pi/agent/pstack/workspaces/--private-var-folders-11-m_kwnqr97632l_cjt0mhytvh0000gn-T-pstack-corpus-ur5cbW-21-PROMPT-HOW-READONLY-EXPLORERS-r2-pi-work--/subagents/2026-11-07T16-53-56-371Z_f94933cf-6841-47c2-b6b2-246475f7e87c.jsonl","pid":null,"machine":null,"description":"Synthesize git storage flow"},"usage":{"input":16880,"output":3899,"cacheRead":19840,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":40619,"cost":{"input":0.06751999999999998,"output":0.07798000000000001,"cacheRead":0.007936000000000002,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.15343600000000002,"totalFromProvider":false}},"isError":false,"durationMs":79543,"time